# /sdd-health

Purpose:
  Validate .sdd/ system integrity: critical files, references, command sync, mojibake, projects purity.

Owns: commands\sdd-health.sdd
Description:
  Validate .sdd/ system integrity. Checks critical files, references,
  graph consistency, and token budgets.

Usage:
  /sdd-health
  /sdd-health --verbose
  /sdd-health --fix

Options:
  --verbose  Show detailed validation results
  --fix      Attempt to fix minor issues automatically

InitialLoad (Phase 151 — EXPAND protocol):
  - .sdd/INDEX.sdd (routing only)
  - .sdd/runtime/integration-routing.sdd (probe semantics for channel checks)
  Check lists, gates, timeline specs load on EXPAND only.

Checks:
  Critical files exist
  References resolve
  Graph consistency
  Token budgets valid
  Decision ledger valid
  No corrupted files
  Chain graph integrity
  Evolution health (temporal validity, snapshots, migrations)
  Channel health (Phase 150): external integrations probed per
    runtime/integration-routing.sdd — 4-way probe classification
    (missing/broken/timeout/error), active_backend resolution,
    tier-grouped report (0=zero-config, 1=key/login, 2=setup);
    one failing channel degrades to its own row, NEVER crashes the report
  3-way command sync (Phase 152): every .sdd/commands/*.sdd spec has
    its .claude/commands/<name>.md and .kilo/command/<name>.md wrappers
    ([CMD8]/[R98]) — any missing pair is a WARN drift finding
  Mojibake scan (Phase 152): repo text files scanned for UTF-8-as-CP1252
    sequences (the canonical double-encoded em-dash triplet and CP1252
    vowel signatures — signature list lives in the scanner code, not here,
    so this spec never trips itself) — hits are CRITICAL findings ([R99])
  Projects purity (Phase 152): .sdd/projects/ holds ONLY real instances
    + the {project_name}/ template; foreign folders are WARN findings
    ([R105])
  SW1 chain integrity (Phase 159): .sdd/chains/swarm.sdd exists and its
    16-stage flow keys match .sdd/workflow/step-keys.sdd (SW1 group) and
    .sdd/workflow/stages.sdd (UNIT/UNIT_TS/E2E/E2E_TS/FULL/RF-G/FB/REL);
    missing stage or key is a WARN drift finding ([SW1-1])
  Micro-unit sync (Phase 159): .sdd/workflow/micro-unit.sdd entity rules
    are consistent with .sdd/schemas/micro-unit.sdd and the FocusLoop
    bounds in .sdd/chains/swarm.sdd; mismatch is a WARN finding
  Phantom command detection (Phase 159): scan .sdd/workflow/*.sdd for
    /sdd-* command definitions that are NOT registered in
    .sdd/commands/INDEX.sdd; each phantom is a WARN finding ([CMD8])

Output:
  HEALTHY | DEGRADED | UNHEALTHY | FAILED
  Channel section (Phase 150): per-channel status + active backend
  + broken-install prescription (reinstall hint) per probe semantics.
  With list of warnings or errors.

Exit Codes:
  0 - Healthy
  1 - Degraded
  2 - Unhealthy
  3 - Failed

Rules:
  [HEALTH-01] /sdd-health MUST check critical file existence first.
  [HEALTH-02] /sdd-health MUST verify all @references resolve.
  [HEALTH-03] /sdd-health MUST validate chain graph cycle detection.
  [HEALTH-04] /sdd-health MUST check temporal validity of snapshots.
  [HEALTH-05] /sdd-health MUST probe external channels with real
              execution (not existence) per [IR-02]; retries only for
              transient statuses ([IR-05]).
  [HEALTH-06] A channel probe failure degrades that channel's row —
              it MUST NOT fail the whole health report ([IR-06]).
  [HEALTH-07] Channel probe output MUST pass credential scrub before
              rendering ([IR-07]).
  [HEALTH-08] 3-way registry sync: spec/wrapper count mismatches and
              missing .claude/.kilo wrappers are WARN findings ([CMD8]).
  [HEALTH-09] Mojibake hits are CRITICAL findings; the report is UNHEALTHY
              until fixed ([R99]).
[HEALTH-10] Foreign folders under .sdd/projects/ are WARN findings
    ([R105]); the {project_name}/ template dir is expected.
  [HEALTH-11] SW1 chain integrity: swarm.sdd flow keys must match
    step-keys.sdd (SW1 group) and stages.sdd; missing stage or key is
    a WARN finding ([SW1-1]).
  [HEALTH-12] Micro-unit sync: micro-unit.sdd, micro-unit schema, and
    swarm.sdd FocusLoop bounds must agree; mismatch is a WARN finding.
  [HEALTH-13] Phantom command detection: any /sdd-* defined in
    .sdd/workflow/*.sdd but missing from .sdd/commands/INDEX.sdd is a
    WARN finding ([CMD8]); --fix rewrites them as REDIRECT notes.

Navigation:
  INDEX: @INDEX.sdd
  ChainGraph: @../chains/graph.sdd
  SwarmChain: @../chains/swarm.sdd
  References: @../references/INDEX.sdd
  Timeline: @../timeline/INDEX.sdd
  IntegrationRouting: @../runtime/integration-routing.sdd

State: +
   (enhanced with evolution health checks per Phases 130-134)
   (extended with channel health probing per Phase 150, Agent-Reach
    probe/doctor patterns — MIT, cited in integration-routing.sdd)

# Reading discipline (reference)
Follows CLAUDE.md Reading Strategy: goal-first, grep-before-read, ead(offset,limit) slices, Read Plan when >=2 files or >250 lines, stop at goal.
